CRE workflow registration
├── when linking to CRE
│   ├── only Symbiotic's current registry owner can link
│   ├── permit linking independently of workflow acceptance
│   ├── failed linking permits retry
│   ├── no off-chain request authorization entry point exists
│   └── registration failures preserve the link and pending proposal
├── after linking
│   ├── reject linking while already linked upstream
│   ├── allow both owner addresses to rotate without changing registrations, proposals or the CRE owner link
│   ├── keep Symbiotic proposal authority and curator acceptance authority separate after rotation
│   ├── retain standard ownership renunciation without changing workflows or pending curator acceptance
│   ├── the provider can propose, replace or cancel pending proposals
│   └── additional Oracles and replacements still require curator acceptance
├── given a provider proposal
│   ├── only the registry owner can propose, replace or cancel it
│   ├── only the current Oracle owner can accept it
│   ├── expose the exact workflow ID and all registration fields in storage
│   ├── replacement overwrites all fields and cancellation clears them
│   ├── require the exact nonzero ID and unchanged artifact metadata
│   ├── permit proposals before the Oracle is governed by this registry
│   └── account roles and ownership grant no workflow acceptance authority
├── when accepting a workflow
│   ├── register the wrapper-owned ACTIVE workflow using the Oracle's canonical name
│   ├── store the accepted ID per Oracle without writing Oracle storage
│   ├── allow curator acceptance without reading the Oracle's pinned registry
│   ├── compare inputs with the stored ID and every registration field
│   ├── update the existing record with a fresh ID and clear the full proposal atomically
│   ├── tolerate a missing previous registration after upstream deletion
│   ├── reject paused-workflow reactivation, DON changes and already registered IDs
│   ├── keep normal rotation available after upstream quota reductions
│   ├── retain NAV, snapshot and limits
│   ├── preserve the cached rejected report and permit review while it remains fresh and newer
│   ├── preserve expired NAV without refreshing its timestamp
│   ├── reject old-workflow reports through the real forwarder
│   └── preserve all state when Chainlink registration fails
├── given two Oracles using the registry
│   ├── isolate curator acceptance, names and active registrations
│   ├── reject globally duplicated IDs without deleting the original
│   └── changing one registration leaves the other reporting
├── isolated gas snapshots
│   ├── link success and expired-link rejection
│   ├── first registration and subsequent replacement
│   ├── proposal creation, replacement, cancellation and mismatched acceptance
│   └── configured and empty dynamic proposal reads
└── when interacting with Chainlink owner administration
    ├── reject registration until linked
    └── upstream unlinking deletes registrations and permits relinking with a fresh proof

Cancellation events
└── emit empty parameters when clearing a pending proposal and preserve active registration
